From: Haldexx
Subject: [PATCH] memfd: let MFD_ALLOW_SEALING clear F_SEAL_SEAL

The donor kernel's memfd_create() backport looks up the new file's
shmem_inode_info but drops the upstream (3.17) line that clears F_SEAL_SEAL
for MFD_ALLOW_SEALING. shmem_get_inode() starts every inode with
F_SEAL_SEAL, so every memfd was born sealed against further seals:
F_GET_SEALS returned F_SEAL_SEAL and F_ADD_SEALS failed with EPERM.

Perfetto needs SHRINK|GROW|SEAL on its shared memory buffers. Measured on
the SM-N920I with tests/memfd_probe.c (aarch64 and 32-bit compat).

---
diff --git a/mm/shmem.c b/mm/shmem.c
--- a/mm/shmem.c
+++ b/mm/shmem.c
@@ -3032,6 +3032,8 @@
 	info = SHMEM_I(file->f_path.dentry->d_inode);
 	file->f_mode |= FMODE_LSEEK | FMODE_PREAD | FMODE_PWRITE;
 	file->f_flags |= O_RDWR | O_LARGEFILE;
+	if (flags & MFD_ALLOW_SEALING)
+		info->seals &= ~F_SEAL_SEAL;
 
 	fd_install(fd, file);
 	kfree(name);
